narrative:
The omens arrive without spectacle: a well that tastes of iron, sheep standing still in rain, a dawn that refuses to brighten. The Piebald Fool sits on a mile marker, feeding crumbs to no birds.

@Piebald Fool: What was buried, borrowed breath. What was broken, learns to walk.

Resistance-Warden Iska Vell is already marking safe houses on a map.

The Dark Legion crosses the fields without raising dust. Its Herald wears a smooth mask and speaks in a voice that sounds painfully familiar, though no one can say whose. The first occupied village goes silent behind shut doors.

@Herald Unbound: You called this realm yours. It did not agree.
@Iska: Then we make it disagree with you.
